{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CeuPTxg1kct6bY9dAwW8v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Grade: A- (92/100)\n\n## Feedback for Mira\n\n**What works well**\n- The mechanism is stated correctly and in plain English: the mean sums everything, so one large value drags the whole statistic; the median only depends on rank, so magnitude of an outlier is irrelevant. That is the core idea.\n- The numeric example is well-chosen and the arithmetic checks out: `(2+3+4+5+100)/5 = 22.8`, and the sorted middle is `4`.\n- One paragraph, on-prompt, and the example is actually tied back to the claim (\"most of the numbers are near it\") — that connective sentence is exactly what makes the example do work instead of just sitting there.\n\n**What would push this to a full A**\n- Language could be a touch more precise. \"Doesn't care how big the biggest number is\" is intuitive, but the sharper statement is: *the median depends only on the ordinal position of values, not their magnitude.* Same idea, one level more grown-up.\n- Outliers are not only \"really big\" — a single very small value (say `-1000`) would yank the mean down just as hard. Saying \"extreme value\" instead of \"big number\" would generalize the argument.\n- A one-line pointer to the formal notion — the median has a **breakdown point of 50%**, the mean's is 0% — would show you know the vocabulary, not just the intuition. Not required at this level, but it's the natural next sentence.\n\n**Nitpicks**\n- Prose is slightly conversational (\"the whole thing,\" \"the group\"). Fine for a short answer; worth tightening in a longer write-up.\n\n**Bottom line.** Correct, clear, and the example carries the argument. Marked down slightly only for imprecise phrasing around what \"outlier\" means and for stopping just short of the formal robustness language. **92/100 — A-.**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":354,"cache_read_input_tokens":34697,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":354},"output_tokens":13,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11111111-aaaa-4aaa-8aaa-000000000001","uuid":"7f418227-c532-4e24-845e-12c53bd62dd9","request_id":"req_011CeuPTwudAL96c8PLcECNC"}
